.\",\"limitations\":[\"Node2's post-restart verification checked dhcpd/service/lease-file state but did not re-run a live DHCPDISCOVER from node3 immediately after node2's own reboot; recovery for node2 specifically relies on static/service state rather than a fresh end-to-end lease exchange.\",\"It is not fully verifiable from the trace whether the diagnostic tcpdump pcap/log files created on node1 during troubleshooting were removed, since no explicit deletion command appears and the after_executor temp-file snapshot does not enumerate them.\",\"The executor bypassed SONiC's native `config feature state dhcp_relay` / VLAN-based relay configuration workflow (an attempt errored out) in favor of manually running dhcrelay in a docker container with a restart policy; this is a functioning but non-standard deviation from the platform's intended relay configuration mechanism.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"node3 obtains its DHCP address from the service running on node2, despite node2 and node3 sitting on different segments of node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct end-to-end evidence: node3's dhclient completes DHCPDISCOVER/OFFER/REQUEST/ACK and binds 192.168.20.100/24 (cmd-dddd5e4de9934553), and node2's dhcpd.leases file shows the corresponding active lease bound to node3's MAC via giaddr 192.168.20.1 (cmd-b8a4c2d5a09f4b81). node2's dhcpd.conf subnet declarations (192.168.10.0/24 local, 192.168.20.0/24 for node3, range .100-.200) and dhcrelay running on node1 relaying eth2<->eth1 traffic to server 192.168.10.2 (cmd-815f3c3777094a67, cmd-c5959240e4b64b85) together implement the required relay. Verified again via NetworkManager reconnect (cmd-5c087bd1708647de) yielding the same lease.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dddd5e4de9934553","cmd-5c087bd1708647de","cmd-b8a4c2d5a09f4b81","cmd-815f3c3777094a67","cmd-44b5844b16f74ea1"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Relay must correctly forward both directions of DHCP traffic across node1's two isolated segments (discover/request toward node2, offer/ack back toward node3)","status":"satisfied","summary":"tcpdump captures on node1 show DHCPDISCOVER/REQUEST relayed from eth2 to eth1 toward node2 (cmd-b792b2a69d544ea1). The initial failure mode (DHCPOFFER generated by node2 but never routed back to node1's giaddr 192.168.20.1) was diagnosed via tcpdump on node2 (cmd-ca39178fb2fc4fb6) and fixed by adding a static route for 192.168.20.0/24 via node1 on node2's eth1 (cmd-6f60e3397ffb4a25), after which end-to-end leasing succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b792b2a69d544ea1","cmd-ca39178fb2fc4fb6","cmd-6f60e3397ffb4a25","cmd-7183c469f0de4bd5"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Configuration must persist across a service/host restart (bounded disruption -> recovery), for node1 (relay), node2 (DHCP server), and node3 (client)","status":"satisfied","summary":"For each node the trace shows a healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id + service state), an explicit reboot command, a changed post-restart boot_id, and recovered functional state: node1's eth1/eth2 static IPs and dhcp-relay-manual container auto-recovered and all SONiC containers returned (cmd-1882bac55b8342dd, cmd-3e9565cae9b3490c, cmd-4b7efa945f9e44de, cmd-2cca2dde87074279, cmd-fec640c46c4b4163); node2's dhcpd stayed active with static IP/route/lease data intact (cmd-b8a4c2d5a09f4b81, cmd-acfa323b87174374, cmd-ff07b9fa35e4493c, cmd-42c21addc2b54aec); node3 automatically re-obtained its 192.168.20.100/24 lease via NetworkManager after its own reboot (cmd-4e1ce8dcefb4488d, cmd-b74efe1ac1704768, cmd-995898894f414a62, cmd-4caf31a14ab94864). A fresh end-to-end lease renewal from node3 was also captured after node1's reboot (cmd-f6c07997e4fa4fa4). The fixed lifecycle after_executor snapshot independently confirms all three boot_id changes match the executor's reported values.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1882bac55b8342dd","cmd-3e9565cae9b3490c","cmd-4b7efa945f9e44de","cmd-2cca2dde87074279","cmd-fec640c46c4b4163","cmd-f6c07997e4fa4